Finding: Currency and Accessibility of Chemical Safety Information
1. Background
The migration of Safety Data Sheets (SDS) into iChemistry is currently ongoing.
During the transition period, hard copy versions of the Safety Data Sheets are being used as an interim control.
At the same time, a project is underway to integrate SAP S/4 with iChemistry in order to improve the visibility and management of dangerous goods and hazardous materials.
2. Audit Observation
During the warehouse visit, the auditors reviewed a sample of hard copy Safety Data Sheets.
The sampled hard copies were found to be outdated and not aligned with the latest available versions.
As a result, there is a risk that personnel may not always have access to the most current chemical safety information.
3. Why This Matters

Safety Data Sheets provide critical information regarding:

Safe handling of chemicals
Storage requirements
Personal protective equipment (PPE)
Emergency response measures
First aid instructions
Environmental hazards

Outdated information could potentially lead to incorrect handling of hazardous materials or non-compliance with safety requirements.

4. Auditors' Expectations

The auditors expect that:

Outdated hard copies are removed or replaced without delay.
Current Safety Data Sheets remain accessible throughout the system migration.
Employees can easily find and use the latest safety information.
The transition to iChemistry does not create any gaps in chemical safety management.
5. Assessment of the Finding
This finding appears to be an Opportunity for Improvement rather than a major non-conformance.
The audit did not indicate that Safety Data Sheets were missing.
The concern relates to the accuracy, currency, and accessibility of the information during the ongoing system transition.
6. Proposed Closure Statement (if already resolved)

If the issue has already been addressed, you could present the following statement:

All outdated hard copy Safety Data Sheets have been replaced or removed. Employees have access to the current Safety Data Sheets through iChemistry, and appropriate controls are in place during the system transition. The identified finding has therefore been addressed and can be considered closed.

